      "type": "paragraph",
      "heading_path": [
        "Buyer's Guide Basis of payment - Types of basis of payment",
        "Buyer's Guide"
      ],
      "markdown": "Types of basis of payment There are four main types of basis of payment used in contracts and it is possible to use multiple types in one contract. These include: fixed price options: fixed price competitive fixed price non-competitive fixed price subject to economic price adjustments fixed time/unit rate with or without an economic price adjustment cost reimbursable options, with: no fee fixed fee target cost / incentive fee fee based on actual costs provisional price When choosing the types of basis of payment to use for a contract there are many items to consider, including: clarity of the scope and requirements market forces contract duration price validation contractor readiness applicability of incentives Note : A contract using a fixed time/unit rate or a cost reimbursable basis of payment must include either a ceiling price or a limitation of expenditure.",
      "plain_text": "Types of basis of payment There are four main types of basis of payment used in contracts and it is possible to use multiple types in one contract. These include: fixed price options: fixed price competitive fixed price non-competitive fixed price subject to economic price adjustments fixed time/unit rate with or without an economic price adjustment cost reimbursable options, with: no fee fixed fee target cost / incentive fee fee based on actual costs provisional price When choosing the types of basis of payment to use for a contract there are many items to consider, including: clarity of the scope and requirements market forces contract duration price validation contractor readiness applicability of incentives Note : A contract using a fixed time/unit rate or a cost reimbursable basis of payment must include either a ceiling price or a limitation of expenditure."
